      "totalDuration": "1 yr 4 mos",
      "description": "- Maintained and supported the growth of the teams AWS serverless Global Submission API for large commercial insurance, which processes approximately 40,000 submissions per month.\n- Directed the build-out of a new transformation service to retire the companies core submission service, resulting in an immediate estimated annual savings of $46,000 and approximately 5,000 business hours. The new service utilizes AWS serverless infrastructure such as API Gateway, Lambda, SQS with a DLQ, EventBridge, and ElastiCache, written using TypeScript.\n- Led the team's effort to integrate our Global Submission API into the company’s Data Lake, so that data is centralized for future analytical and AI purposes.\n- Overhauled a critical design flaw in our TCOR service by making a process shift to automatically failover when we experience an outage with an external service. This enables over 60 employees to continue sending submissions to underwriting, thereby preventing revenue loss for large accounts.\n- Acted as a secure DevOps role model by collaborating with the cybersecurity team to mitigate threats for code vulnerabilities and exposed secrets, ensuring the company meets the NY DFS compliance mandates to maintain business operations in New York.",
